1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
kick a pebble and let it
fly until it gets there.

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,360
To Kashiwa from P.E.,
who was clowning around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as I was.

5
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:36,140
What's so good about this energy?

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
As a man, I'm dead serious,
and that's all there is to it.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,020
One nightmare that never changes.

8
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,900
The streets are kinder than ever.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:48,980
The crows are cawing, so let's head home.

10
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,860
Is there really yakitori?

11
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:11,120
Thank you for watching.

12
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,380
Also, this unexpected day

13
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:34,620
Even if it's just an
internal station newsletter,

14
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:37,940
it's all wedding and family
articles about officers.

15
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:41,600
Nobody would be happy to see my hobbies,
I don't think.

16
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:44,540
The only one who'd be happy
is the person featured in it.

17
00:01:44,540 --> 00:01:46,600
I think making it is just a waste, though.

18
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:50,860
Because of that, we end up with a
pile of returns like this every month.

19
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:53,160
The reason I called you two
here is none other than this.

20
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:57,620
With our young, fresh sense,
something the officers would happily read,

21
00:01:57,620 --> 00:02:00,600
I want you to make the
Monthly Katsushika report.

22
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,820
You want us to make it?

23
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:05,200
Yes. Won't you take it on?

24
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,760
Sounds fun, doesn't it? Let's do it.

25
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:08,980
Yeah, I guess.

26
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:11,760
Understood. We'll take it on.

27
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:17,760
It's the first issue after the renewal, so
let's do something flashy and splashy, right?

28
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:22,980
In that case, how about a feature on Nakagawa,
the number one handsome guy everyone in the station wants to marry?

29
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:28,380
And while we're at it,
the man nobody wants to marry,

30
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,780
Ryotsu Kankichi, who's been number one for 20 years straight,
would make a fun feature too, don't you think?

31
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,900
Yeah, yeah,
if we put those two front and center,

32
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,780
everyone's attention is guaranteed.

33
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:39,140
Then I'll write the article on Nakagawa.

34
00:02:39,140 --> 00:02:42,660
Hey, wait!
I'm the one interviewing Nakagawa.

35
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:44,980
Reiko, you cover Ryotsu Kankichi.

36
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:46,240
No way, I'm not doing that.

37
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:54,020
Fine. No hard feelings,
let's settle it with rock-paper-scissors.

38
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,740
Fine. Here we go.

39
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,000
Rock, paper, scissors!

40
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,180
Yes!

41
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:03,380
What rotten luck.

42
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:08,440
Don't be so disappointed. You can churn
out piles of articles about that lowlife.

43
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:14,320
Now I'm going to thoroughly expose
every lowdown thing about Kankichi Ryotsu.

44
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,860
This smell is irresistible.

45
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:27,180
Thinking about it, the week until payday

46
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:30,580
was a miserable stretch of
nothing but bread crusts and water.

47
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:34,480
A proper meal for the first time in a week.

48
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:35,720
I'm going to dig in big time!

49
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,060
Plate, plate...

50
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:42,460
We still haven't gotten a decisive photo opportunity,
have we?

51
00:03:47,280 --> 00:04:10,160
Hehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehehe...

52
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:10,940
This...

53
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:12,160
Hey, wait!

54
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:14,720
Hey!

55
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:16,360
Come on, hey!

56
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:18,000
Whoa!

57
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,320
Damn cat!

58
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:26,780
Hey, get back here!

59
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,340
Give me back my saury!

60
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,320
Ow ow!

61
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:32,840
Whoa!

62
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:37,000
Cut it out, annyeong!

63
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:38,660
Whoa!

64
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,900
You bastard! Stop! Stop!

65
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,034
Damn it,

66
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:56,380
the last one got burnt to a crisp too.

67
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,320
This is the worst.

68
00:05:11,820 --> 00:05:14,280
Why is it so noisy this
early in the morning?

69
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:18,460
Chief! Something terrible happened.
Please take a look at this!

70
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,580
Number one on the list of
men nobody wants to marry.

71
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:26,180
A day in the life of Kankichi Ryotsu,
the absolute worst.

72
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:29,980
Who on earth put this photo in
there without anyone noticing?

73
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,580
Is that man Ryo-san?

74
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,760
Looks like it.

75
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,100
What are those guys doing?

76
00:05:35,100 --> 00:05:37,640
They're the new recruits
who joined this spring.

77
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:40,020
Hey, hey, stop jabbering on
about people behind their backs!

78
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,840
Whoa, here he comes!

79
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,320
Looking at us like we're
something disgusting.

80
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:47,780
He vanished in an instant, didn't he?

81
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:48,337
Damn it!

82
00:05:48,387 --> 00:05:51,880
Only those two would pull a stunt like this.

83
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,420
What's this all of a sudden?

84
00:05:56,420 --> 00:06:00,120
Don't play dumb!
You wrote this article, didn't you?

85
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,920
It wasn't me!

86
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:03,080
Look.

87
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,720
The one I covered was this one,

88
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,560
and yours was Naoko.

89
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,960
Naoko Damn you.

90
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,200
Hey, Naoko!

91
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,440
It's Ryotsu Kankichi.

92
00:06:18,440 --> 00:06:21,440
How dare you put up such a
photo and humiliate me like this!

93
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,980
Why are you getting so worked up?

94
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,960
I just captured you as you really are.

95
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:29,720
It's your own fault for
being so awful all the time.

96
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:34,100
Even so, secretly taking
pictures like that is cowardly!

97
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:36,480
Besides, it's an invasion of privacy!

98
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,100
I'm going to knock you flat!

99
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:40,180
Let go of me! Don't stop me!

100
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,760
It wasn't me, senpai!

101
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,520
Chief! Station chief!

102
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,540
You idiot!

103
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,680
There's no need to get so angry.

104
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:55,020
Of course I'd shout!
What's the meaning of this?

105
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,660
Let's hear your explanation.

106
00:06:57,680 --> 00:07:01,540
That's why I'm protesting that
it's an invasion of privacy.

107
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,120
No, it's this photo.

108
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:08,580
Did you eat the park's carp
knowing it was forbidden?

109
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:13,220
No, that 30,000 yen that was stolen...
I just gave in on impulse.

110
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:16,100
You, come here!

111
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,920
Forgive me!

112
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:22,520
Shut up and come quietly!

113
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,220
He lectured me for three hours!

114
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:35,300
Damn it, this is all Naoko's fault.

115
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:38,500
If it's come to this,
I'll get my revenge thoroughly!

116
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:41,040
Ozaki, good work.

117
00:07:45,100 --> 00:07:48,480
Senpai, why do I have to do this too?

118
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,720
Stop complaining and let's go.

119
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:26,200
So this guy was working part-time
at a shady-looking place like this?

120
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:29,180
No way, that can't be true, surely.

121
00:08:29,180 --> 00:08:32,900
No, there's no mistake.
Right, I'll get the definitive photo!

122
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:38,760
Senpai,
there's no way this is going to work.

123
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,900
This is the only way to blend in, right?
You wait here.

124
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,140
It's absolutely impossible, though.

125
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,200
Excuse me.

126
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:56,780
That's not it.
I came because I saw the help-wanted sign.

127
00:08:57,700 --> 00:09:01,020
You're joking, right? I'm totally serious.

128
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:09,560
We don't like freaks here. Look in the mirror, you're something else.
No, he's in the class! Thank you very much.

129
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,480
Ah!

130
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:19,960
I'll call the boss, yes.

131
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:28,460
So what was it? It's a video rental. He came to return a video he rented,
apparently. Yeah.

132
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:31,140
Honestly,
you walked into such a misleading place.

133
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:38,120
Hi, John!

134
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:41,260
Hi, Naoko!

135
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:43,960
Good evening, how are you?

136
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:45,940
I'm fine, thank you.

137
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:47,860
They look pretty close, don't they?

138
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,214
I thought she had no interest in men,

139
00:09:50,264 --> 00:09:52,560
but she's been seeing a foreigner like that?

140
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:54,920
They're going into a café!

141
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,360
Let's go, Honda!

142
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,420
Yes sir!

143
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:03,160
"Ekimae Nyūgaku, Nabauunagi"

144
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:05,460
Hey, lend me that costume for a second.

145
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,420
Welcome!

146
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:14,460
There they are, over there, coffee!

147
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,620
Yes, certainly.

148
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,240
Thank you for waiting.

149
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:37,760
Damn, I can't understand
a word you're saying.

150
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:40,920
Are you okay, senpai?

151
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:41,814
Yes,

152
00:10:41,864 --> 00:10:45,860
it's because of the Milky
Fine that's trendy on weekends.

153
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:49,397
P-p-please,

154
00:10:49,447 --> 00:10:51,440
One more!

155
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:54,800
Thank you for waiting.

156
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:01,520
Delicious.

157
00:11:05,040 --> 00:11:07,920
See you again next week. Bye.

158
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:08,980
Bye.

159
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,760
That was pretty quick.

160
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,120
Thank you very much.

161
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:15,640
Hey, you.

162
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:16,540
What?

163
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:20,960
So how about you and Naoko...

164
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,720
Please, in Japanese.

165
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,580
What, you understand Japanese?

166
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,360
What's your relationship with Naoko?

167
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:31,540
She's my English conversation teacher,
and I'm her student.

168
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,300
Senpai, how did it go?

169
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,880
We were just having an
English conversation lesson.

170
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:44,380
You were taking English conversation lessons?
That's surprising.

171
00:11:44,860 --> 00:11:48,000
Damn Naoko,
she must have some kind of weakness.

172
00:11:48,420 --> 00:11:50,360
I'm going to catch her red-handed,
no matter what.

173
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:00,080
Eeeeeeh!

174
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,560
There she is, there she is!

175
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:13,440
Naoko's bound to let loose today,
since she's off duty.

176
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:15,560
I'm going to get a perfect photo of her.

177
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:20,040
Senpai, why do I have to dress
as a woman just to tail her?

178
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:23,660
Well, if we were men, people would
mistake us for stalkers, wouldn't they?

179
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:27,420
I think we'd look a lot
more suspicious this way.

180
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,660
Stop your griping and let's go.

181
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,280
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

182
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:42,740
Where is Naoko headed? Didn't she say her family home is in Yokohama?
She's not going home to visit, is she?

183
00:12:42,740 --> 00:12:45,460
Isn't she? Anyway, let's drop this disguise.

184
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:54,760
What are you two laughing at?
That seat is for the elderly!

185
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:58,940
Young people should stand.
It's better for your health, you know.

186
00:12:58,940 --> 00:12:59,380
Yes, ma'am.

187
00:13:00,660 --> 00:13:02,180
Young people these days...

188
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:04,600
We're not even on the train, old man!

189
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,560
Inside the train, inside the train!

190
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:29,000
Hayako-chan, cheese, cheese

191
00:13:30,220 --> 00:13:32,040
Looks like they're meeting up, doesn't it.

192
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:35,580
Senpai, please stop talking like that.
It's creepy.

193
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,600
What did you say?

194
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,860
Someone's coming.

195
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,340
What?

196
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:45,060
What, so you were dating that brat?

197
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:49,320
They look pretty serious, don't they.

198
00:13:49,980 --> 00:13:52,220
W-what? Is it already a breakup talk?

199
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:57,380
What a clingy woman.

200
00:13:57,380 --> 00:13:59,060
Honda, we're going too.

201
00:13:59,060 --> 00:13:59,980
Yes, indeed.

202
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,040
No way!

203
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:16,640
Seriously?!

204
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,540
Mamoru!

205
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:22,120
Johnny, I'm counting on you for the Eiroken.

206
00:14:24,460 --> 00:14:27,780
Mamoru! Hanging around a place like this,

207
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:29,020
Come on, let's go home.

208
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:30,040
Let go of me!

209
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:30,860
Mamoru!

210
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:35,998
That Mamoru guy,

211
00:14:36,048 --> 00:14:39,560
you've been pestering me
and I'm fed up with it!

212
00:14:39,560 --> 00:14:41,860
It's none of your business!

213
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:44,940
What a feisty woman.

214
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:52,180
Come on, you two, get out of here too.

215
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:54,180
If you don't, you'll be in serious trouble.

216
00:14:54,180 --> 00:14:54,860
Hey!

217
00:14:55,540 --> 00:14:57,500
What are you doing? Let go of me!

218
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,440
Come with me.

219
00:14:58,440 --> 00:14:59,760
I said, let go!

220
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:00,880
Calm down!

221
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,100
We'll hear your story somewhere quiet,
so come on.

222
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:08,340
Things are starting to look shady,
aren't they?

223
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:09,100
Yeah.

224
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:13,760
Look closely and you're actually pretty cute

225
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,680
Unless you want to scar that face of yours,

226
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:16,780
get lost already.

227
00:15:16,780 --> 00:15:20,120
Do you two have any idea who I am?

228
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,120
I'm a cop.

229
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:23,860
Think we're scared of the police?

230
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:25,200
Don't make me laugh,
we can keep up this tough act.

231
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:28,700
Bring it on, then.

232
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,620
You're worthy opponents for us.

233
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:41,800
This is bad, boss. Let's go help them.

234
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:42,520
Wait!

235
00:15:44,280 --> 00:15:45,120
Stop it!

236
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:47,380
Mamoru, you're pretending to be the leader.

237
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:51,780
I asked you to chase them off,
not to use violence.

238
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,100
Shut up!

239
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,160
Mamoru, are you okay?

240
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:58,060
What do you think you're
doing to my little brother?

241
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:00,980
Your brother? So he really is your brother.

242
00:16:01,420 --> 00:16:04,700
Mamoru,
you never said a cop was your sister!

243
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,920
You two really tricked us.

244
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,500
We're going to beat you two senseless,
both of you together.

245
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:13,520
Hold on a second!

246
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,920
W-what are you two?

247
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:19,040
We're just passing-by college girls.

248
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:19,700
Hehe.

249
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,160
G-gross.

250
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:25,380
How rude!

251
00:16:25,380 --> 00:16:27,760
If you keep using
violence on those brothers,

252
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,940
we big sisters won't stand for it!

253
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,980
Some weirdos showed up

254
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:34,120
Hey, take these guys out first!

255
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:53,500
!

256
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:56,100
If you come one step closer, this woman -

257
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,380
Nice!

258
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:09,420
Well done, senpai!

259
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:10,740
Easy, easy!

260
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,440
You'd better remember this.

261
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:28,960
Ryotsu Kankichi, I'll thank you for now.

262
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:30,880
Gah, how did you figure it out?

263
00:17:31,220 --> 00:17:32,420
Senpai, your wig! Your wig!

264
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:33,660
Damn, we're busted.

265
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:36,680
Anyway, what are you two doing around here?

266
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:37,945
W-well, that's ah...

267
00:17:37,995 --> 00:17:41,020
Yes, right,
there's a cosplay party near here.

268
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,460
Hey, Hayako-chan.

269
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:43,580
R-right.

270
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,360
So you two have that kind of hobby?

271
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,820
Hey, forget about me.
Why are you mixed up with those people?

272
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:51,980
I was about to ask you the same thing.

273
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,380
I was trying to get
Mizuki out of that group.

274
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,340
Mizuki?

275
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:02,960
Mizuki Kimura.

276
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:06,180
The girl who used to come
over to our house a lot?

277
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:10,740
Ever since her parents divorced last year,
she's been kind of reckless.

278
00:18:11,300 --> 00:18:13,480
I noticed she'd stopped
coming to high school too,

279
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:15,200
and it turns out she's been
running around with those guys.

280
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,040
So I pretended to join them,
trying to get her out of that group.

281
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:23,980
If that's the case,
why didn't you just tell us honestly?

282
00:18:23,980 --> 00:18:25,980
Her mother was worried sick, you know.

283
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:30,560
Mamoru, you like that Mizuki girl,
don't you?

284
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:33,420
It's not like that. He's a good guy.

285
00:18:33,420 --> 00:18:36,100
Ever since he was a kid,
he's loved animals and flowers.

286
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:39,660
Then why don't you tell
him directly to stop?

287
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,640
I did, but...

288
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:43,480
Shut up.

289
00:18:43,900 --> 00:18:46,060
You shouldn't hang out
with people like that.

290
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,040
You couldn't possibly understand how I feel.

291
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:50,080
Just leave me alone already.

292
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:51,380
Mizuki.

293
00:18:54,140 --> 00:18:54,860
Mizuki.

294
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,020
I wanted to understand how he feels.

295
00:18:59,020 --> 00:19:01,220
So you joined their gang?

296
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:04,840
What a good little brother.

297
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:06,520
He's still just a kid.

298
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:09,100
Alright, Mamoru,
can you put your life on the line?

299
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:14,120
Sometimes a man has to put his life
on the line for someone important.

300
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:16,760
I'm asking whether you
have the courage for that.

301
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:18,180
I do.

302
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:21,120
Got it. Then leave the rest to me.

303
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:26,220
Johnny

304
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:31,060
Jim! Don't worry!
We didn't come here to beat you up again!

305
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:34,200
Mamoru wants a direct match with you!

306
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:34,780
What?

307
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:39,540
Are you crazy?
Mamoru can't possibly beat Johnny!

308
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:41,940
You can't know that until you try!

309
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:44,400
You've got some nerve!

310
00:19:44,900 --> 00:19:45,900
I have a condition.

311
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:48,597
If Mamoru wins,

312
00:19:48,647 --> 00:19:52,180
I want that girl to get out of your group!

313
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:53,580
Is that all right?

314
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,240
No way! Why should I have to...!

315
00:19:57,560 --> 00:20:00,220
Then if I win,

316
00:20:00,730 --> 00:20:08,540
I'll run naked through the streets of Yokohama!
Interesting, I accept that challenge!

317
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:09,520
Yeah.

318
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:23,900
What's wrong? You're not done yet.

319
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:32,260
It's impossible.

320
00:20:32,260 --> 00:20:34,860
That girl has never once been in a fight.

321
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,300
Bear it, Naoko.

322
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:40,140
If you walk out now,
everything will be ruined.

323
00:20:40,560 --> 00:20:42,260
Then it's over.

324
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:48,860
Why, why would you do something this stupid?

325
00:20:49,840 --> 00:20:52,420
It's for the promise between you and me.

326
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:53,300
Promise.

327
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:56,220
From when we were in elementary school.

328
00:20:59,480 --> 00:21:02,640
I've been thinking about becoming
a veterinarian when I grow up.

329
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:03,560
Mm.

330
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:06,920
Mizuki, you love animals,
so you'll definitely make it.

331
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:07,920
Really?

332
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:09,520
Really.

333
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:11,280
Thanks, Mamoru.

334
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:13,360
I'm definitely going to become one.

335
00:21:14,020 --> 00:21:14,740
I'll cheer you on.

336
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:15,820
It's a promise.

337
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:17,260
Yeah, a promise.

338
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:22,620
So that Mizuki can make her
childhood dream come true.

339
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:35,840
It's over

340
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,020
I haven't lost yet.

341
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:47,060
It's not over yet.

342
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:51,880
What a guy.

343
00:21:52,420 --> 00:21:53,800
Holy crap, this is bad.

344
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:59,420
Hey, you won.

345
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:00,320
Mizuki

346
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:04,080
You're free. Do whatever you want.

347
00:22:05,260 --> 00:22:05,920
Alright, let's go.

348
00:22:07,780 --> 00:22:08,640
Mamoru

349
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:11,180
Pull yourself together, Mamoru!

350
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:18,140
Mamoru, I'm sorry. All of this was for me.

351
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:20,060
I'm really sorry.

352
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:21,080
It's fine.

353
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:22,860
Ryo-san

354
00:22:23,740 --> 00:22:24,100
What?

355
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:25,180
Me?

356
00:22:26,440 --> 00:22:28,400
I got a good look at that.

357
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,760
You won.

358
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:32,060
You're a real man among men.

359
00:22:40,020 --> 00:22:41,060
Naoko.

360
00:22:42,060 --> 00:22:43,280
Kankichi Ryotsu.

361
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:44,800
Good work.

362
00:22:45,700 --> 00:22:47,740
Naoko, how's Mamoru been since then?

363
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:50,460
His injuries have healed,
and he's already back to full strength.

364
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:51,480
I see.

365
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:52,660
What about Mizuki?

366
00:22:53,140 --> 00:22:54,880
I hear she's going to school properly now.

367
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,180
Thank you so much.

368
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:58,500
I've changed my opinion of you too.

369
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:01,120
You were quite the caring big sister.

370
00:23:01,980 --> 00:23:04,080
Stop it, Kankichi Ryotsu!

371
00:23:04,080 --> 00:23:04,680
Senpai!

372
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:07,320
Senpai, it's an emergency!

373
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,260
What's wrong?

374
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:11,400
Th-This, p-please look at this!

375
00:23:12,540 --> 00:23:13,460
W-what is this?

376
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:15,480
And now Nana-chan's looking at me weird.

377
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:17,140
What are you going to do about this?

378
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:18,120
Naoko.

379
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:20,840
Senpai.

380
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:22,340
Hey.

381
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:25,940
Naoko, what is the meaning of this?

382
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,100
Here, you left your camera in Yokohama,
didn't you?

383
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:30,660
Come on, let's go, Komachi.

384
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:31,240
Yeah.

385
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:34,220
See ya!

386
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:36,100
Hey, get back here!

387
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:39,620
Damn it, you'll pay for this.

388
00:23:39,620 --> 00:23:43,060
I'm definitely going to take embarrassing photos of you,
you hear me?

389
00:23:52,500 --> 00:23:57,840
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

390
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:04,560
Walking while looking back,
holding Gāja's hand

391
00:24:05,680 --> 00:24:11,700
That strange feeling I had back then

392
00:24:12,540 --> 00:24:16,960
So, the tiles of the arcade street

393
00:24:16,960 --> 00:24:22,740
I tried walking only on the black ones

394
00:24:25,240 --> 00:24:31,020
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

395
00:24:31,940 --> 00:24:38,340
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too

396
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:44,000
Go on, turn that corner

397
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:49,100
You can meet everyone, everyone

398
00:24:50,040 --> 00:24:53,760
Over there is Kame-ari

399
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,100
Surely Kame-ari

400
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:02,300
Come on over, everyone, to our town!

401
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:06,980
Over there, there are turtles,

402
00:25:07,940 --> 00:25:10,220
surely there are turtles.

403
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:15,400
Come on over, everyone, to our town!

404
00:25:16,660 --> 00:25:17,020
Thank you.

405
00:25:20,580 --> 00:25:23,700
Nakagawa,
are you really going to quit the police?

406
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:26,600
I see. If you've decided that,
I won't stop you.

407
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:30,260
But in return, become a fine
successor to the Nakagawa Group,

408
00:25:30,260 --> 00:25:33,340
and hire me as your secretary
at a high salary, okay?

409
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:37,180
Next time:
"The Nakagawa Family Inheritance." Look forward to it!

410
00:25:45,420 --> 00:25:49,240
Come on over, everyone, to our town!

411
00:25:50,200 --> 00:25:50,880
Thank you.

